# Week 3 – Exploratory Data Analysis & Feature Engineering

## Objective
The objective of this week is to analyze the dataset to understand relationships between input features and crop yield, and to prepare the data for machine learning model training.

## Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
EDA was performed to gain insights into the dataset and identify important patterns. The following analyses were carried out:

- Visualization of relationships between independent variables and crop yield
- Analysis of rainfall, temperature, and soil nutrient levels
- Identification of correlations between features
- Detection of missing values and outliers

## Important Features Identified
Based on EDA, the following variables were found to significantly influence crop yield:
- Nitrogen (N), Phosphorus (P), and Potassium (K) levels
- Rainfall
- Temperature
- Soil type
- Crop type
- Season

## Feature Engineering
The following feature engineering techniques were applied:
- Encoding categorical variables such as soil type and crop name
- Creation of new features like:
  - Growing season index
  - Number of heat days
  - Average seasonal rainfall
- Normalization and scaling of numerical features

## Outcome of Week 3
- Key relationships between features and yield were identified
- Important variables affecting crop yield were determined
- Dataset prepared for model training through feature engineering
